\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "fig:The-interpretability-gap"

\end_inset

The interpretability gap is visualized, metaphorically, by a deep trench
 that lies between man and machine.
 It represents the learning effort of an individual to understand what a
 black box policy is doing.
 The land on which humans stand further represents a space where communication
 and teaching is possible, so that the expert can relate to beginners and
 theoretically teach them techniques to improve.
 The gap is not equally difficult to cross everywhere; the more prior knowledge
 one has, the smaller the gap in things that need to be understood.
 The expert stands at the narrowest point, yet the trench still has to be
 crossed.
 We want to automatically create artificial solutions that function as steppings
tones for the expert, which should be as similar as possible to the expert
 policy while having the performance of the black box.
 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

