\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{Genetic programming}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is an evolutionary optimization method that generates functional programs
 to solve a given task.
 It was first introduced by Koza and has since become a popular method for
 creating interpretable system controlling policies 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Koza_GP_patent_1990"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Evolutionary algorithm require a representation of candidate solutions as
 combination of genes as well as a fitness function which rates their performanc
e in solving the task.
 GP represents programs as programming trees, which allow random evolutions
 like mutations or recombination of genes between candidates (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:crossover"

\end_inset

).
 
