\begin_layout Subsection
Offline Fitness Function: Symbolic Regression 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "Symbolic-Regression"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The fitness function determines how well a candidate solves the task.
 To train on offline data, symbolic regression can be performed.
 This evaluates the mapping of mathematical expressions around a data set
 using the regression error.
 Two regression metrics were used for this work.
 The mean average error (MAE) is defined as the average deviation from the
 target solution and is true to distance.
 The mean squared error (MSE) squares the individual deviations, which is
 harder to interpret, but penalizes outliers more which can lead to better
 overall generalization.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
begin{eqnarray*} 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
text{MAE} & = & 
\backslash
frac{1}{n}
\backslash
sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_{i}-
\backslash
hat{y}_{i})
\backslash

\backslash
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
text{MSE} & = & 
\backslash
frac{1}{n}
\backslash
sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_{i}-
\backslash
hat{y}_{i})^{2} 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
end{eqnarray*}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To obtain an authentic regression error, it may also be necessary to map
 the result values to the closest possible value in the action space before
 calculating.
 For example, in the case of a bounded action space, a value must be mapped
 to the interval (
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$a_{
\backslash
text{bounded}}=
\backslash
max(
\backslash
min(a,A_{max}),A_{min})$
\end_layout

\end_inset

), and in the case of a discrete space, rounding would be required (
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$a_{discrete}=
\backslash
lfloor a
\backslash
rceil$
\end_layout

\end_inset

).
 A possible adjustment of the MSE is visualized in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
