\begin_layout Subsection
Simple If-Acceleration with a Fixed Core
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:eval-fixed"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In response to the limitations of the TED preserving familiar structures
 in trees with only few nodes, a fixed core was defined in the aforementioned
 if-acceleration policy.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The obligatory distinction between action 0 and 2 is no actual drawback,
 but since the SARSA policies both choose action 1, the regression error
 can no longer be reduced to 0.
 With the SARSA-200 limit being 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$0.023$
\end_layout

\end_inset

, the regression error could still be reduced to 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

