\begin_layout Subsection
SARSA-75 Black Box
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This section examines the effects of the poorly trained SARSA-75 black box
 agent compared to the SARSA-200 version, without addressing the Pareto
 candidates of each run.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
At 75 training episodes, the SARSA agent did not yet manifest the strategy.
 Its behavior is uncertain in many states, which leads to a larger observation
 space.
 For example, the data features a rollout which failed shortly before the
 target, resulting in state samples that do not occur with the SARSA-200
 policy.
 The regression error is reduced at best to 0.2 for all MSE runs MAE runs
 performed worse in terms of both regression error (
\begin_inset ERT
status open

