\begin_layout Subsection
Explorative Regression
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Explorative-Regression"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In a regular regression, only the deviation from the target value can be
 considered.
 With trusted GP, it is additionally possible to include the deviation from
 the previous policy.
 A smaller deviation from the known is easier to trust, especially in safety-cri
tical domains.
 Such an exploratory regression examining phenotypic similarity can be implement
ed in many ways.
 For example, a subdivision into 4 intervals is possible, as seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:relative_kernel_path"

\end_inset

.
 A more radical version that prevents deviations in the wrong direction
 can be seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:exploression-regr1"

\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Considering the interval between the familiar and AI solution 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$|(y_{
\backslash
text{f}})|$
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and the deviation from the familiar solution 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$(y_{
\backslash
text{f}}-
\backslash
hat{y})$
\end_layout

\end_inset

, the following conceivable formula results, which evaluates the resulting
 4 ranges differently and can be considered as independent of the normal
 regression error.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\sum\max(0,|(y-y_{\text{f}})|-(y_{\text{f}}-\hat{y}))
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
However, combining both paradigms into one regression value is very difficult
 to train.
 Therefore, it is advisable to set up another Pareto front where additional
 trade-offs can be made.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\align center
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename img/inkscape/explorative_regression_hill.pdf

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
An example of the importance of different explorations, where the goal is
 to find the best way up a mountain.
 The blue path represents the known and familiar path, with the area marked
 in blue where we are still comfortable.
 The green one is a faster AI solution whose deviation is evaluated in a
 regression so that path (1.) and path (2.) would be equally good.
 However, (1.) requires less behavioral change, which is preferable from
 a trust perspective.
 Apart from this, we can assume that path (3.) is almost certainly a wrong
 exploration, since it goes even further away from the target solution,
 starting from the known path.
 Finally, (4.) deviates early in an area where the target solution was already
 well approximated and also influences the subsequent strategy.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "fig:relative_kernel_path"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


